gaER(){return"Refresh prices to load sector data"},
gaES(){return"Each row replays your real buys & sells \u2014 same amounts, same days \u2014 into that holding instead, so the amounts compare directly. Dividends count as cash on both sides: yours, and each target's own payouts. Neither side reinvests them."},
gaET(){return"Reset order"},
aEU(a){return"Reset to "+a+" default layout"},
gaEV(){return"Return on cost"},
gaEW(){return"No snapshot data yet \u2014 returns will appear once the app has recorded at least one daily value."},
gaEX(){return'Portfolio return over each period, calculated from your daily portfolio value snapshots.\n\n\u2022 1M \u2014 last 30 days\n\u2022 YTD \u2014 since January 1st of this year\n\u2022 1Y \u2014 last 12 months\n\u2022 3Y \u2014 last 3 years\n\u2022 5Y \u2014 last 5 years\n\nPeriods show "\u2014" when no snapshot exists that far back (e.g. you started using the app less than a year ago), or when none has been recorded since the period began.\n\nSimple \u2014 total value change from start to end of period. Affected by when you deposited or withdrew cash.\n\nPrice TWR (Time-Weighted) \u2014 removes the effect of deposits and withdrawals, showing how your investments themselves performed. This is the standard way funds report performance.\n\nDividends are not in this figure yet: a payout leaves the portfolio without being counted, so it reads as a fall in value. They count in the Personal IRR card.\n\nTWR shows "\u2014" for a period until the app has recorded enough daily history for it. Shorter periods (1M) fill in first, longer ones (1Y+) as more days are recorded \u2014 so it is always accurate where shown, never estimated. It also shows "\u2014" when, on a day in the period, the portfolio was worth no more than the money added that day \u2014 usually a price that was missing that day.'},
gaEY(){return"Showing full portfolio history (multi-tag selection uses portfolio snapshots)"},
aEZ(a){return'Returns for tag "'+a+'". Price TWR shows "\u2014" for a single tag: it needs the money moved in and out, which only whole-portfolio history records.'},
