gaFr(){return"Search ticker or name \u2014 S&P, Apple, QQQ, BTC\u2026"},
ga5B(){return"Searching\u2026"},
ga5C(){return"Sector Breakdown"},
aFs(a){return"How your portfolio value is distributed across market sectors (Technology, Healthcare, Financials, etc.).\n\nWeighted by current market value in "+a+". Sector data is fetched from Yahoo Finance."},
aFt(a){return a+" \u2014 select a single tag to view this section."},
aFu(a){return"Your good sells saved you "+a+" vs holding."},
gaFv(){return"Set cash"},
gaFw(){return"Add stocks to your Watchlist to see whether you should have bought them instead of (or in addition to) your current holdings."},
gaFx(){return"Compares watched stocks' price returns since you started watching them against your portfolio's average price return (excluding dividends).\n\nBoth figures use price change only, so the comparison is like-for-like. Helps you see which stocks on your watchlist you missed out on \u2014 and whether sitting on the sidelines cost you."},
gaFy(){return"Compares watched stocks' returns since you started watching them against your portfolio's average return over the same period.\n\nHelps you see which stocks on your watchlist you missed out on \u2014 and whether sitting on the sidelines cost you."},
gaFz(){return"Sell or partially trim a stock to see whether you should have held those shares instead."},
gT6(){return"For each stock you've sold (fully or partially), shows what would have happened if you had kept holding those shares until today.\n\nCompares your actual sell price against the current price \u2014 so you can see your biggest regrets and your best exits.\n\nPartial exits show analysis for the shares already sold, independent of the remaining open position."},
aFA(a){return"Show all "+a+" exits"},
a5D(a){return"Show all "+a+" holdings"},
aFB(a){return"Show all "+a+" positions"},
aFC(a){return"Show all "+a+" watchlist stocks"},
ga5E(){return"Show the header and tabs again"},
ga5F(){return"Show less"},
gaFD(){return"Simple avg P/E"},
gaFE(){return"Small Cap (<$2B)"},
aFF(a,b,c){return b+" \xb7 "+c+" shares"+a},
aFG(a){return"Sold "+a},
a5G(a){var s=""+a
return A.aE(a,null,this.a,null,s+" yr",s+" yrs",null,"< 1 yr")},
gaFH(){return"Your portfolio\navg price return"},
gaFI(){return"Watchlist avg\nsince added"},
IV(a){var s=null,r=""+a
return A.aE(a,s,this.a,s,r+" stock",r+" stocks",s,s)},
gaFJ(){return"Avg Change"},
gaFK(){return"Average price change (%) across your watchlist since you started watching each stock, weighted by share price.\n\nWatchlist stocks have no position size, so a higher-priced share carries more weight in this average."},
gaFL(){return"Avg Holding Time"},
gaFM(){return"Avg P/E Ratio"},
gaFN(){return"Avg Watching Time"},
gaFO(){return"Number of different stocks you currently own."},
gaFP(){return"Currency effect"},
aFQ(a,b){return"How much of Total P/L comes from exchange-rate moves rather than the stocks themselves, across your foreign holdings.\n\nTotal P/L is measured in "+a+" against what you paid in "+a+" on each trade date where a dated rate exists. Where none exists, a sell uses the average rate of the holding's buys; anything else uses today's rate, and a note on this card says so. Each holding's own gain or loss (the Locked In and Floating rows when you have partial sells, otherwise just the price move) is measured in its own currency and converted at today's rate. The difference is the currency move on the money you have invested abroad.\n\nFor those holdings: Total P/L = Locked In + Floating + Currency effect \u2212 dividends on shares you have since sold"+b+". Those dividends are inside Locked In, but Total P/L leaves every dividend out, so they are taken back out. All your dividends are under Analysis \u2192 Overview \u2192 Portfolio Quality (Total Dividends Received)."},
gaFR(){return"Current paper gain or loss on the shares you still hold.\n\nThis number changes every time the stock price moves and is only realised when you sell."},
gaFS(){return"Money still at work in your open positions: everything you paid in (buys + commissions) minus what you already got back from any partial sells.\n\nFor positions you have never partially sold, this equals avg buy price \xd7 shares held.\n\nEach trade is converted at the exchange rate of its own date where a dated rate exists, so this number only changes when you buy or sell \u2014 not because of currency movements. Where none exists, a sell uses the average rate of the holding's buys; anything else uses today's rate, and a note on this card says so."},
aFT(a){return"Gain or loss already locked in from shares you have partially sold out of positions you still hold.\n\nThis is money you have actually realised \u2014 it won't change when the stock price moves.\n\nIncludes the dividends paid on the shares you have since sold"+a+", which Total P/L leaves out."},
aFU(a){return" ("+a+" on this card)"},
gaFV(){return"Value-weighted average P/E ratio across your holdings.\n\nP/E = Stock price \xf7 Earnings per share (EPS).\n\nLarger positions have more influence. A higher P/E means the market expects more growth; a lower P/E may indicate the stock is cheap \u2014 or that growth is slow."},
gaFW(){return"P/L %"},
gaFX(){return"Capital gain/loss as a % of what you invested (dividends excluded).\n\nP/L % = Total P/L \xf7 Total Invested\n\nDoes not account for timing \u2014 see Personal IRR in Analysis for that."},
gaFY(){return"The total cash you received from selling these positions, after selling fees (shares \xd7 sell price \u2212 fees).\n\nConverted at today's exchange rates."},
gaFZ(){return"Locked-in profit or loss from closed positions, including any dividends received.\n\nRealized P/L = Total Proceeds \u2212 Total Invested + Dividends\n\nConverted at today's exchange rates, so this figure can drift slightly with currency moves after the sale."},
